# error_case_return — error variant creation and return
# (README §9). Tests building and returning error values.

ErrorCaseReturn is project
ErrorCaseReturn module examplesErrorCaseReturn
ErrorCaseReturn target console
ErrorCaseReturn entry main

examplesErrorCaseReturn is module
examplesErrorCaseReturn path examples.errorCaseReturn
examplesErrorCaseReturn exports main
examplesErrorCaseReturn purpose "Demonstrate error case creation and return"
examplesErrorCaseReturn invariant "Error variants are properly typed"

MyError is error
MyError case failure Int32
MyError case timeout

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Create and return an error value"
main invariant "Error case construction works"

main let result immutable Int64 1
main let okCode immutable ExitCode 0

main do printResult
main return okCode

printResult is call
printResult in main
printResult invokes console.writeIntegerLine
printResult arg value Int64 result
